---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Why this site exists.">
  <section class="page">
    <h1 class="font-display page__title">About Chronicles Uncovered</h1>
    <div class="prose-article">
      <p>
        This site began from a love of history — particularly the history of Sabah and North
        Borneo, Malaya and Malaysia, and Southeast Asia more broadly. It exists to tell the
        stories that get flattened into a single sentence in most retellings: the difference
        between 1957 and 1963, why Brunei stayed out of Malaysia, what actually happened during
        the Japanese occupation of North Borneo, and the disputes historians and governments
        still don't agree on.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every article tries to separate established fact from mainstream interpretation,
        disputed claims, political or legal positions, legend, and deliberate counterfactual
        speculation — labelled inline, not blurred together. Sources are listed at the bottom of
        every piece, and primary documents (treaties, archives, government records) are
        preferred over secondary summaries.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is a personal, ongoing project. Articles move through research notes, drafts, and
        fact-checking before publication — you may see that status marked on a piece if it isn't
        finished yet.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: 3rem 1.25rem 4rem;
  }
  .page__title {
    color: var(--color-paper-50);
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
